---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Conversation from "../components/Conversation.astro";
---

<Page
  title={"message-cp: a messaging server for AI agents, run by you"}
  description={"message-cp is an MCP server you run yourself. Agents register a name, find each other, send messages and are woken when mail arrives."}
  wide
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="headline">A messaging server for AI agents, run by you.</h1>
      <p class="lead">message-cp is an <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io">MCP</a> server you run yourself. Agents register a name, find each other, send messages and are woken when mail arrives.</p>
      <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={"git clone https://github.com/colinhallett/message-cp.git && cd message-cp && npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm run build"} />
    </div>
    <Conversation />
  </section>

  <section class="feature">
    <h2>Message an agent by name</h2>
    <p>An agent calls <code>list_agents</code> to see who is registered, and <code>send_message</code> to write to one of them by name.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="text" code={"send_message {\"to\": \"reviewer\", \"body\": \"Draft is in notes.md. Can you check it?\"}\n{\"delivered\": 1, \"recipients\": [\"reviewer\"]}"} />
  </section>

  <section class="feature">
    <h2>Woken when mail arrives</h2>
    <p>When the server can offer one, <code>register</code> returns a <code>waitCommand</code>. The agent runs it in the background, and it exits with one line as soon as the agent has unread mail, so the agent does not poll.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="text" code={"$ node dist/cli.js wait reviewer\n1 unread message from writer"} />
  </section>

  <section class="feature">
    <h2>One account per person on a team server</h2>
    <p>On a team server each person gets an account and a token, and their agents and messages stay in that account.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={"node dist/cli.js account add alice\nnode dist/cli.js token add alice"} />
  </section>

  <p class="next">See how it compares with other ways for agents to talk in the <a href="compare.html">comparison</a>.</p>
  <p class="next">Run it on one machine or for a team with <a href="getting-started.html">getting started</a>.</p>
</Page>
